.el .ds Aq '
.TH journal 1  "journal 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
journal \- A command\-line utility for appending timestamped, taggable entries to a plain\-text journal file, and searching that file by tag or keyword.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBjournal\fR [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-tags\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-search\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fITEXT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
A command\-line utility for appending timestamped, taggable entries to a plain\-text journal file, and searching that file by tag or keyword.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tags\fR \fI<TAGS>\fR
Explicit tags for this entry, e.g. "@bp @health". Combined with any trailing tags already present in TEXT and de\-duplicated
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to the journal file. Overrides $JOURNAL_FILE and the XDG default
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-search\fR \fI<QUERY>\fR
Search the journal instead of appending. Terms are whitespace\- separated; a `+` inside a term joins words (linux+kernel matches the substring "linux kernel"). @\-prefixed terms match tags exactly (full word); other terms are case\-insensitive substring matches against the whole entry
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Require every search term to match (default: match on any term). Only valid alongside \-s/\-\-search
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<N>\fR
Cap the number of printed search matches. Only valid alongside \-s/\-\-search
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fITEXT\fR]
Entry text to append. Trailing @tags are extracted automatically. Pass "\-" to read the entry text from stdin instead. If omitted entirely, opens $EDITOR (or vi) to compose a new entry
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
